    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n### 1. **governance.test.js - Missing named exports** \nThe test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./index.js`, but it was only available through the default export. I added named exports for:\n- `APPROVAL_STATUSES`\n- `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`\n- `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`\n- `RISK_LEVELS`\n\nThis resolved the error: `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'join')`\n\n### 2. **eval/index.test.js - Incorrect metric parameters**\nThe `runEvaluations` function was calling all metrics with both outputs and references, but `toxicityMetric` only accepts outputs (its second parameter is for custom banned terms, not references). I updated `runEvaluations` to check each metric's arity (`function.length`) and call it appropriately:\n- Metrics expecting 1 parameter get only outputs\n- Metrics expecting 2+ parameters get both outputs and references\n\nThis fixed the toxicity score being 0 instead of 1.\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files\n\u2705 All existing public exports preserved\n\u2705 No breaking changes to the API",
